WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.835 --> 00:00:01.910
(audience applaud and cheer)

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:02.910
- Thank you.

00:00:03.862 --> 00:00:04.937
- I like your jacket.

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:07.080
- I did it for you.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.760
- [Kelly] Yeah, well thank
you, dressing up for Christmas.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.593
I love Christmas.

00:00:09.593 --> 00:00:11.610
We just did Rockefeller together.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.516
- We did.

00:00:12.516 --> 00:00:13.349
- Do you love Christmas?

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:14.520
Do you get into the whole spirit of it?

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.629
- Yes, I do.

00:00:15.629 --> 00:00:16.620
- [Kelly] Yeah, me too.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.870
- Yeah, but you know, when I was a kid,

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.620
my stepfather brought home
the first Christmas tree

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.645
that I'd ever had 'cause he
had just come into my life.

00:00:25.645 --> 00:00:26.478
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:26.478 --> 00:00:29.280
- [Barry] And it was a little
aluminum foil Christmas tree

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.900
with blue balls, and I thought it

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.730
was the most beautiful
thing I'd ever seen.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:34.440
- Oh, I love that.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.931
I love that that memory sticks too.

00:00:35.931 --> 00:00:36.956
- [Barry] Yeah.

00:00:36.956 --> 00:00:38.097
- How special.

00:00:38.097 --> 00:00:38.930
- You never know, see,
people always think you have

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:39.763
to go big and extravagant,

00:00:39.763 --> 00:00:41.490
but that little Charlie Brown
moment, that's so beautiful.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:42.510
I love that.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:43.800
- [Barry] Yeah, well, we had no money.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:44.910
- [Kelly] Yeah, no me.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:45.743
We didn't either.

00:00:45.743 --> 00:00:47.040
That's, yeah, so I'm with you.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.436
But your Christmas special
airs tonight on NBC, right?

00:00:49.436 --> 00:00:50.269
- Yeah, and it's great.

00:00:50.269 --> 00:00:51.154
- [Kelly] Are you excited?

00:00:51.154 --> 00:00:51.987
(audience applauds)

00:00:51.987 --> 00:00:53.700
I love, I love doing Christmas specials.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.973
Look at all that talent on this stage.

00:00:55.973 --> 00:00:57.240
- [Barry] I know, it's great.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.860
- [Kelly] Yes.
- [Barry] It's a great show.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:01.320
I was able to put in some of the hits

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.510
and the Christmas songs

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.820
and you don't even know
which one is coming,

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:06.653
and it's really great.

00:01:06.653 --> 00:01:07.680
- [Kelly] Oh, I like that.
- [Barry] Yeah.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.020
- Oh, that's really cool to
do because people always want,

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.610
yeah, they always wanna
hear like the hits as well,

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.600
so that's really smart.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.433
- Yeah.

00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:14.937
- I'm not that smart,
I've never done that.

00:01:14.937 --> 00:01:16.293
(Barry laughs)
(audience laugh)

00:01:16.293 --> 00:01:17.490
But we heard that they
wouldn't let you have puppies,

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:18.620
that you wanted puppies.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.740
- Well yeah, how did you know that?

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:20.573
- [Kelly] They didn't, I know.

00:01:20.573 --> 00:01:21.406
Well, I like puppies.

00:01:21.406 --> 00:01:22.408
- Well, you know,

00:01:22.408 --> 00:01:23.241
I've got everything man.

00:01:23.241 --> 00:01:24.074
It snows on the audience

00:01:24.074 --> 00:01:27.810
and there's presents and
there's trees and I thought,

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.010
and little children,

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.560
the little kids come
running out and Santa Claus,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.700
- Magical.
- [Barry] Everything.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:33.570
So we had everything,

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:36.570
and I said, gee, wouldn't it
be great if we had like a puppy

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.100
for one of the little kids?

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:38.933
- [Kelly] Wouldn't it be great?

00:01:38.933 --> 00:01:40.320
Let's bring Barry a puppy.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:41.542
He didn't get a puppy.

00:01:41.542 --> 00:01:42.929
(audience cheers)
(bells jingling)

00:01:42.929 --> 00:01:43.762
We've got puppies.

00:01:43.762 --> 00:01:44.646
Look at these two cute puppies.

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:46.833
(audience cheering)
(bells jingling)

00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:48.657
(Barry laughing)

00:01:48.657 --> 00:01:50.118
Oh my God.

00:01:50.118 --> 00:01:51.473
Can I hold one?

00:01:51.473 --> 00:01:52.709
- Oh my goodness.

00:01:52.709 --> 00:01:54.044
- [Mandy] This is Spot.

00:01:54.044 --> 00:01:55.068
(Kelly exclaims)

00:01:55.068 --> 00:01:56.081
- [Barry] Oh, how old are they?

00:01:56.081 --> 00:01:56.914
- Hi.

00:01:56.914 --> 00:01:58.225
- [Mandy] And this is Tiny.

00:01:58.225 --> 00:01:59.249
- Oh goodness.

00:01:59.249 --> 00:02:00.143
- Hello.

00:02:00.143 --> 00:02:00.988
- [Barry] Oh my goodness.

00:02:00.988 --> 00:02:01.821
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.696
- What's your name?

00:02:03.696 --> 00:02:04.529
Oh he's little.

00:02:04.529 --> 00:02:06.660
- [Kelly] Barry, this is dangerous.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.163
I do not need another dog.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.820
Oh my God, everybody, I should
mention these puppies are

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.730
Spot and Tiny from the
Brixies Rescue Center.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.500
And you can find out
how you can adopt them

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.103
or their friends by heading to
our shows Instagram stories.

00:02:19.103 --> 00:02:19.950
- [Barry] Oh, aren't you the sweetest.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.260
- [Kelly] You're sweet.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.670
Hello.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.503
Hello.

00:02:24.503 --> 00:02:25.683
- I think she recognizes me.

00:02:25.683 --> 00:02:26.516
- [Kelly] She did.

00:02:26.516 --> 00:02:28.287
She was like, Mandy's her favorite.

00:02:28.287 --> 00:02:29.724
- Do you have all my albums?

00:02:29.724 --> 00:02:30.557
Mandy is her favorite.

00:02:30.557 --> 00:02:32.230
You're trying to get
to my coffee, bruh, no.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:34.073
I hear that you

00:02:34.073 --> 00:02:36.570
actually ended up
breaking Elvis's record in

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.280
Vegas with the most live shows, right?

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.113
- That was great.

00:02:39.113 --> 00:02:39.946
It was an honor.

00:02:39.946 --> 00:02:40.779
- [Kelly] That's insane.

00:02:40.779 --> 00:02:41.841
- It really was an honor.

00:02:41.841 --> 00:02:43.470
- [Kelly] 'Cause anytime
people think of Vegas,

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.630
you think of Elvis and
all those live shows.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:46.463
- [Barry] Yeah.

00:02:46.463 --> 00:02:47.296
- And you have trumped him, I like it.

00:02:47.296 --> 00:02:50.850
- [Barry] Yeah, and you know,
on that day I sang Hound Dog.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:51.710
- [Kelly] Oh, did you?

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:52.950
- Me singing Hound Dog.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:53.783
- [Kelly] Why not?

00:02:53.783 --> 00:02:55.470
- And I jiggled around a little bit, like.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.593
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:56.593 --> 00:02:57.426
I like it.

00:02:57.426 --> 00:02:59.040
You gotta jiggle a little, it's Elvis.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:02:59.880
Oh, they're like crying.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.620
Do you wanna go run around?

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.790
Maybe they wanna run around.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:03.952
I don't know.

00:03:03.952 --> 00:03:04.785
- Should we do it?

00:03:04.785 --> 00:03:05.618
- Do you want down or do you want,

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:06.451
do you want down?

00:03:06.451 --> 00:03:07.284
- You wanna,

00:03:07.284 --> 00:03:08.117
- We're gonna let them down.

00:03:08.117 --> 00:03:08.950
- [Barry] You want to go down?

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:09.783
- Let 'em free.

00:03:09.783 --> 00:03:10.616
Let 'em be free.

00:03:10.616 --> 00:03:11.449
- Okay.

00:03:11.449 --> 00:03:12.282
Okay, ready?

00:03:12.282 --> 00:03:13.115
- Here we go.

00:03:13.115 --> 00:03:13.948
- Ready, run.

00:03:13.948 --> 00:03:14.781
- Go have fun.

00:03:14.781 --> 00:03:15.614
- Okay.

00:03:15.614 --> 00:03:16.447
- They're gonna be peeing
all over this place.

00:03:16.447 --> 00:03:17.610
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:18.510
- Ready pee.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.280
- Yeah, go.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.620
They're like, this is mine, this is mine.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:25.020
So while they're marking their territory,

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.100
oh my God, they're so cute.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.006
I really don't need another dog, Barry.

00:03:28.006 --> 00:03:29.910
But I'm thinking about it.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:30.743
So you,

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.060
I've actually celebrated my
birthday a few times on stage.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.260
It just so happens that it happens.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.166
But you just did your 80th
birthday on stage, right?

00:03:36.166 --> 00:03:36.999
- I know, 80.

00:03:36.999 --> 00:03:37.832
Can you believe that?

00:03:37.832 --> 00:03:38.665
(audience applauds)

00:03:38.665 --> 00:03:39.498
- It's, you know what?

00:03:39.498 --> 00:03:40.331
It flies by.

00:03:40.331 --> 00:03:41.308
You don't feel your age.

00:03:41.308 --> 00:03:42.141
- No.

00:03:42.141 --> 00:03:42.974
- Yeah.

00:03:42.974 --> 00:03:44.160
- No, I don't.
- Yeah.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.380
- It's crazy, it's crazy.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:47.460
- I heard you did something funny

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.690
when you came out on stage.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:49.523
- I did.

00:03:49.523 --> 00:03:50.370
(Barry laughs)

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.870
I walked out with a walker like this,

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.150
(audience laughs)

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.220
and then I got to the edge of the stage

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.380
and I went, Ta-Da!

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.940
It's a miracle.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.590
- [Kelly] Oh my God, that's amazing.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:03.000
It is, it is so funny though.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:03.930
I'm with you though,

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.550
I don't feel 41, either.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:06.533
I don't feel,

00:04:06.533 --> 00:04:08.612
- [Barry] 41, you're a
baby compared to this.

00:04:08.612 --> 00:04:09.445
- [Kelly] I know, but no,

00:04:09.445 --> 00:04:10.530
I'm saying though,
like, when we were kids,

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.240
you know, I remember I being 10,

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.470
I'd be like, oh, they're almost dead.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:14.303
Like, you know what I'm saying?

00:04:14.303 --> 00:04:15.750
Like, you're literally in your head.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.640
But like now I'm like,
it doesn't feel that way.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.020
You don't feel, I think you're

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.204
as young as you wanna feel.

00:04:20.204 --> 00:04:21.037
- You know what the trick is?

00:04:21.037 --> 00:04:22.740
I just don't stop.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.120
I just keep going.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.620
There's always another project

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:28.713
and another song and another album.

00:04:28.713 --> 00:04:32.280
And I think if you slow
down, you're gonna stop.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.910
And I'm not about to stop.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:35.470
- [Kelly] Yeah, and why you love it?

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:36.303
- [Barry] Yeah, I love it.

00:04:36.303 --> 00:04:37.200
- It's music and you love it.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.340
Yeah.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.763
I agree with you.

00:04:39.763 --> 00:04:43.140
Is it true that same stepdad
got you an accordion.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:44.130
Did he get you an accordion?

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.623
Is that your first musical
instrument that you got?

00:04:45.623 --> 00:04:47.640
- It was, I'm afraid to say, yes.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.200
- Do you ever play it on stage?

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.317
'Cause I really want to see it.

00:04:50.317 --> 00:04:51.150
- I do.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.196
I did a little section where I played

00:04:53.196 --> 00:04:54.947
'Like a Virgin'.

00:04:54.947 --> 00:04:56.190
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.023
- [Barry] Right.

00:04:57.023 --> 00:05:00.090
And 'Born in the USA'
and it was just awful.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.229
Just awful.

00:05:01.229 --> 00:05:02.062
And it was funny.

00:05:02.062 --> 00:05:03.060
- [Kelly] If awful means wonderful.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:04.230
Yeah, I know.

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:05.670
That's why I love your personality.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.410
You're like this really
incredibly talented guy,

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.771
but also very witty.

00:05:08.771 --> 00:05:11.940
I heard that your first,
your first job was

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:13.261
actually in the mail room at CBS.

00:05:13.261 --> 00:05:14.094
- Yeah.

00:05:14.094 --> 00:05:14.927
- Like in the entertainment world.

00:05:14.927 --> 00:05:15.760
- I was.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:16.593
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:05:16.593 --> 00:05:17.426
- How did you land that?

00:05:17.426 --> 00:05:18.259
That's a random job to land?

00:05:18.259 --> 00:05:19.092
- [Barry] I was lucky.

00:05:19.092 --> 00:05:19.925
I really, I was lucky.

00:05:19.925 --> 00:05:20.758
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:20.758 --> 00:05:21.591
- [Barry] Great job.

00:05:21.591 --> 00:05:22.470
And I met a lot of great people there.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.513
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:23.513 --> 00:05:24.870
- [Barry] And I, the first time

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.180
I ever played a big grand piano

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.635
was in the rehearsal hall at CBS

00:05:29.635 --> 00:05:33.510
and suddenly everybody on the floor

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:37.880
and everybody knew that there's
a piano playing mail boy.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:38.820
(Barry laughs)

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:42.008
And I became the piano
playing mail boy at CBS.

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:42.841
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:05:42.841 --> 00:05:43.674
I love that all those people were like,

00:05:43.674 --> 00:05:46.410
that dude used to rock it
like downstairs on this piano.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.520
And then you're Barry Manilow.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:48.353
That's amazing.

00:05:48.353 --> 00:05:49.710
So congratulations.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.629
You opened Harmony on Broadway.

00:05:51.629 --> 00:05:52.462
- Yeah.

00:05:52.462 --> 00:05:53.603
- [Kelly] This has been a long
time in the making, right?

00:05:53.603 --> 00:05:54.630
- Yes, yes.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:57.030
It's been 30 years.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:57.870
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:58.787
- [Barry] Yeah.

00:05:58.787 --> 00:05:59.620
- We started,
- [Kelly] Labor of Love.

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:00.453
- [Barry] About 30 years ago

00:06:00.453 --> 00:06:01.950
and we mounted it a couple of times,

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:03.840
but we just couldn't get it into New York.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.398
But now, we did.

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:06.231
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:07.064
- We got it into New York.

00:06:07.064 --> 00:06:07.957
- [Kelly] Congratulations.

00:06:07.957 --> 00:06:08.813
(Kelly and audience applauds)

00:06:08.813 --> 00:06:10.380
- Alright, well we have a review here.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.930
Barry hasn't seen this yet,
but we wanted to show him.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.840
So this expert is from
the New York Stage Review.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:17.430
Be advised not even to run,

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:21.720
but to race to this tale of a
Six Man Berlin singing group

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:23.220
that was founded in 1927.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:24.053
That was awesome.

00:06:24.053 --> 00:06:24.886
And then we have another one,

00:06:24.886 --> 00:06:27.210
the New York Times, which
also listed the musical

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.010
as a critic's pick,

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:32.400
said Manilow's vocal arrangements
written with John O'Neill,

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.050
the show's music director are marvelous.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:36.131
I mean, who's shocked at
that news, New York Times.

00:06:36.131 --> 00:06:36.964
(applause)

00:06:36.964 --> 00:06:38.310
You would be the one

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:40.260
to write incredible arrangements.

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:41.401
- Yeah.

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:42.330
- [Kelly] That's amazing
though, for people to see it

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.610
and love it and like get people to go.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:47.340
- Yes, it's a very, very important

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.100
and very deep show and very funny.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:51.840
- Oh I love, I wouldn't doubt

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.360
with you being involved,
this is crazy too.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.700
Did you ever, I heard
this could be a joke,

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.070
but did you write into Playboy for advice,

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:00.570
like career advice?

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:03.480
Yeah. And what kind of career
opportunity was one looking

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:04.863
for writing into Playboy?

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:08.370
- I was a desperate young guy.

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.930
- Okay, okay.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.990
- Yeah. I didn't know what
to do with my musical life.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:16.290
And so I saw this thing
in Playboy magazine.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:20.159
My stepfather, I guess used
to buy it and I sent...

00:07:20.159 --> 00:07:21.213
- You just outed him. I like it.

00:07:21.213 --> 00:07:25.380
- Yeah, right. So I sent a
letter saying, I have an offer

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:28.560
to go on the road with,
with a girl singer.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:31.710
I played piano and in
order to do that, I had

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:34.920
to leave my job at CBS as the mail boy.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:35.753
- Which is steady work.

00:07:35.753 --> 00:07:36.900
- Which one should I do?

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:37.733
- Yeah.

00:07:37.733 --> 00:07:39.540
- And they, they wrote me
back and they printed it

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:42.712
and they said, take the job outside

00:07:42.712 --> 00:07:45.965
and follow your musical notes.

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:47.693
- Oh I love that.

00:07:47.693 --> 00:07:49.067
- And I did. I left.

00:07:49.067 --> 00:07:50.168
(applause)

00:07:50.168 --> 00:07:51.565
- You left and you did it.

00:07:51.565 --> 00:07:52.500
- I left CBS.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:53.700
- So really you have Playboy

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.020
to thank for everything.

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:56.520
- I do. No, I do.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:58.410
- So I know that you and
Bette worked together

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.200
quite a bit, so, did she help
you promote your first album?

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:04.140
- Well, yeah, she let me,
I was her music director.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:04.973
- Yeah

00:08:04.973 --> 00:08:06.393
- And the arranger.

00:08:07.331 --> 00:08:10.920
And we went on the road together
and I had this first album

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.540
and I didn't wanna leave her.

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.760
And so she was very generous,

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:17.520
she let me open her second act.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.740
So instead of her coming out, yeah.

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:24.630
The piano player came out
and you know, that was crazy.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:26.310
The audience didn't wanna see the piano

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.630
player singing three songs.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:31.032
I know that. But again,
they were very kind,

00:08:31.032 --> 00:08:32.100
Bette's audiences were very kind to me.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.933
And they let me do three songs

00:08:33.933 --> 00:08:37.740
and it was the beginning
of my performing career.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:38.910
- Wow. I think you're wrong though.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:40.560
I do think audiences love,

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.870
I have my band do that
sometimes. Like come in and out.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.230
I think they do love seeing
artists support other artists.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:47.063
- Mm.

00:08:47.063 --> 00:08:48.030
- `I think that's a big thing.

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:50.100
- Well she was great to let me do that.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:50.936
- Yeah.

00:08:50.936 --> 00:08:53.100
- And then, you know, then
I actually did take off on

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:55.352
my own and here I am.

00:08:55.352 --> 00:08:57.030
- I know. And then she was like, crap,

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:59.040
I shouldn't have let him.

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.420
I lost my musical director.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:01.774
- Yeah, right.

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:03.725
- That's amazing. So wait,

00:09:03.725 --> 00:09:04.558
- She never forgave me.

00:09:04.558 --> 00:09:07.170
- But you, I love it. She's
like, where the hell did you go?

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:09.870
Like, so wait, so no,
I'm sure she's happy,

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:12.120
but like you, I heard that
y'all were at a bathhouse once.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:13.560
Was it New Year's in the seventies?

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:14.760
- Yeah.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:16.530
- I need to hear this story
because I heard at one

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:17.640
point you took your suit off.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:18.713
What happened?

00:09:18.713 --> 00:09:21.960
- No. It was called The Continental Baths

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:25.530
and she got booked there
and I was her piano player

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:29.340
and it was a spa for, you know, for guys.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.560
- So people are just running
around naked and your singing.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:34.530
- Well, they had towels, you know, around

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:36.300
and she would sing the
Star Spangled Banner.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:39.570
So they would stand up
and the towels would...

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:40.403
- Because she's funny.

00:09:40.403 --> 00:09:41.910
- Check out the merchandising. Yeah.

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:46.731
- Yeah. She's perusing
the menu. It's amazing.

00:09:46.731 --> 00:09:48.180
- It was a great gig, it was a great gig.

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:49.500
- I heard that they got you to jump in.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.197
Is that true? Did you end up jumping in?

00:09:51.197 --> 00:09:53.720
- I did. I jumped. Well they
had a huge pool and it...

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:55.374
- It would be rude not to join.

00:09:55.374 --> 00:09:57.990
- Yeah. It was New Year's
Eve. Everybody was happy.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.490
I, you know, I did.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.350
- I have done that as
well at an after party.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:02.700
I was bored. I was like,

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.080
you know, and I was like, this is boring.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:05.870
So we all jumped in. Me and my band.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:06.703
- Did you take off your
clothes like I did?

00:10:06.703 --> 00:10:07.536
- I did not take off my clothes,

00:10:07.536 --> 00:10:09.870
but I didn't have many
on, I was in my twenties.

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:12.840
I didn't have, I think it
was like a crop top anyway.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.070
- Oh. I was still in my suit and tie

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:15.810
and it all went out and I went in.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:17.910
- I'm kind of a nudist. I don't really,

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:19.170
naked doesn't bother me.

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:21.390
Yeah. Naked doesn't, like
when I went to France

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:23.070
for the first time, I
was so angry I was famous

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:24.000
'cause like I was like, oh,

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.130
people are gonna get
pictures so I can't join.

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:28.380
But I thought it would be so
fun. Everyone was just naked.

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:31.440
And I was like, this is
awesome. I was like, yeah.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.870
- Just go on Naked and Afraid.

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:35.342
- I love Naked and afraid.

00:10:35.342 --> 00:10:36.387
- I love Naked and afraid.

00:10:36.387 --> 00:10:37.220
- Oh my God.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.780
I'm like, what would be your
tool that you would bring?

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:40.613
- Yeah.

00:10:40.613 --> 00:10:41.446
- I would bring an axe.

00:10:41.446 --> 00:10:42.766
I would bring an Axe, I think.

00:10:42.766 --> 00:10:43.599
- Yeah. That's great.

00:10:43.599 --> 00:10:44.670
- You get like one thing, right?

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:45.752
Like I haven't watched it in a while

00:10:45.752 --> 00:10:48.270
- They give you a bowl, you
know, and a fire starter.

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:49.103
- Hell yeah.

00:10:49.103 --> 00:10:50.755
- Those people who can't do the fire..

00:10:50.755 --> 00:10:52.941
- Have you ever started a
fire with just, it's hard.

00:10:52.941 --> 00:10:53.774
- It's hard.

00:10:53.774 --> 00:10:56.067
- Yeah. I would die. Yeah.

00:10:56.067 --> 00:10:58.440
Not the best Girl Scout Barry.

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:00.870
So what, let's talk about
the Manilow Music Project.

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:01.703
Let's talk about that.

00:11:01.703 --> 00:11:02.940
- Well you know, I did that at,

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:06.241
I started about 15 years
ago when somebody's,

00:11:06.241 --> 00:11:08.880
one of my doctors called me

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:10.950
and said, can you get
my daughter a saxophone?

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:13.410
And I said, why? He
said they're running out

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.240
of instruments in her high school.

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:16.830
I said, they're running
out of instruments.

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:18.930
Anyway, when I looked it up, yes.

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:21.270
All the high schools
around the country are

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:22.787
running out of instruments.

00:11:22.787 --> 00:11:23.620
- They cut the arts programs.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:24.453
- All the instruments they have are just

00:11:24.453 --> 00:11:25.286
old and broken down.

00:11:25.286 --> 00:11:27.990
And so I made it my mission to try

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:30.690
to get musical instruments into schools

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:31.710
that are running out of them.

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:34.168
And that's what the
Manilow Music project did.

00:11:34.168 --> 00:11:35.001
(applause)

00:11:35.001 --> 00:11:38.238
- That's so cool. Especially
like, you and I both get it.

00:11:38.238 --> 00:11:41.048
We didn't grow up as much and
I had hand me down everything.

00:11:41.048 --> 00:11:41.881
- Yeah.

00:11:41.881 --> 00:11:42.900
- You know, you, you kind
of survived off that.

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:44.820
And if you wanted to learn,
if you wanted any opportunity

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:47.640
you needed people to have
you know, readily available

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.470
instruments or anything like that.

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:51.300
- These kids are playing
in these, I'm telling you,

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:53.934
broken down instruments
and they still love it.

00:11:53.934 --> 00:11:54.767
- Yeah.

00:11:54.767 --> 00:11:56.160
- They love their music classes.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:56.993
- Yeah.

00:11:56.993 --> 00:12:00.120
- It becomes their second
family. I've met so many.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:00.953
- I was one of those kids. Yeah.

00:12:00.953 --> 00:12:03.300
- Yeah. Somebody, one of the kids sent me

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:05.730
a picture of a tuba that we got him

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:08.190
and the tuba was bigger than he was.

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:09.550
- Which is adorable.

00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:10.890
- He was standing next to it. Yeah.

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:12.643
And that's, that's the kind of thing that,

00:12:12.643 --> 00:12:14.019
that the Manilow Music Project does.

00:12:14.019 --> 00:12:14.852
- Oh, that makes you feel good.

00:12:14.852 --> 00:12:15.685
- Yeah, it's good.

00:12:15.685 --> 00:12:16.518
- Yeah.

00:12:16.518 --> 00:12:17.640
Well go online to find out more about

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.320
the Manilow Music Project everybody.

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:22.350
And be sure to watch Barry
Manilow's A Very Barry Christmas

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:24.693
tonight on NBC for Hits
and Christmas songs.

